This directory vendors Expat 2.9.0, released 2026-10-05.
Source: https://github.com/libexpat/libexpat/releases/tag/R_2_9_0
Source tarball: expat-2.9.0.tar.xz
SHA-256: 1e6371862cc31999b368c3b89b49994f0677e1bab5f1b2b85ae3741f5d803051

The .c and upstream .h files and COPYING come from that tarball's lib/
directory and root, respectively. Coin's expat_config.h is the only
downstream configuration file. It preserves Coin's previous feature profile:
general entities on all platforms, DTD/namespace/context support on Windows,
and /dev/urandom entropy on non-Windows platforms. Coin's CMakeLists.txt
selects the required upstream source files. The obsolete loadlibrary.c from
the previous vendor import is no longer used.

The upstream distribution has additional build machinery, tests, and tools
which are not embedded here. To use a system Expat instead, configure Coin
with USE_EXTERNAL_EXPAT=ON and provide matching system headers and library.
Configuration fails if they cannot be found; it does not silently fall back
to the embedded copy. Coin uses the older Expat location API in this mode,
so a system version predating 2.9.0 remains possible.

The embedded Expat 2.9.0 uses C99 language features. Upstream officially
supports MSVC 2022 and newer; its CMake emits a warning, not an error, for
MSVC 2019. Coin does not impose MSVC 2022 as a minimum, but the embedded
copy has not been validated with the MSVC 2019 compiler/toolset. MSVC has no
C99 language mode, so Coin's C_STANDARD=99 target property does not itself
prove compatibility. The current Windows CI uses MSVC 2022. Validate both
Expat modes with the actual MSVC 2019 toolset before claiming that either
build is compatible with it.
